WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:05.710
Rent is due, you've got bills, and there’s
no sign of a pay check coming anytime soon.

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:09.640
So, maybe if you’re a government worker,
it's time to find a second job?

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:14.130
The Fairfax county school district outside
of Washington DC has a shortage of substitute

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:15.200
teachers.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.680
And Fairfax County now has an excess of furloughed
government workers.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:21.800
Problem, solution ... at least temporarily.

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:36.360
"About 20% of the population in the greater
dc area works for the federal government...this

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:40.899
local community saw an opportunity to do something
their people."

00:00:40.899 --> 00:00:45.730
When the school district advertised the event,
it filled up to capacity within 24 hours.

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:50.700
The interest was so overwhelming that they
added a second, and then a third hiring day.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:55.180
While it usually takes a few weeks to approve
new substitute teachers, these people will

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:58.010
all be processed and ready to work in just
a few days.

00:00:58.010 --> 00:01:01.020
The school board says, it’s really the least
they can do.

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:15.549
"Our employees here realized that we have
a lot of workers in need....and give them

00:01:15.549 --> 00:01:18.799
an opportunity to earn a paycheck."

00:01:18.799 --> 00:01:34.740
"We've heard lots of teachers are thrilled
to have the influx of talent ... it will have

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:37.599
a positive effect on our students."

00:01:37.599 --> 00:01:40.349
The shutdown could end at any time.

00:01:40.349 --> 00:01:45.400
Many federal employees at the event said they're
doing ok for now, but in the meanwhile, they

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:49.849
want a contingency plan, and the whole situation
is disheartening.

00:01:49.849 --> 00:02:04.249
"I endured the 2013 shutdown...this one's
a little more

00:02:04.249 --> 00:02:09.849
frustrating because there's no discussion,
or very little discussion."

00:02:09.849 --> 00:02:19.890
"I'm frustrated, because I think services
to the citizens are being compromised..."

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:48.510
Where the federal government is stuck in the
mud, its employees are moving on, and this

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:52.089
local government is stepping up to help them.

